d butchery is a gentle trade. But you do owe it to your daughter—and to your own peace of mind—to judge the man himself, not just the apron he wears. Let him show you whether that toughness has a soft side. If it doesn't, you'll have real evidence to bring to your daughter, not just a stereotype. That's not naive. That's the sharpest kind of wisdom there is.
