eeping your eyes open. Your wife's unease, your grandfather's words, your own instincts—they're not wrong. They're a valuable warning system. But a warning system tells you to *watch*, not to *condemn*. Watch him closely. If he turns out to be the hard-hearted man the old saying predicts, you'll see it soon enough, and you'll have something real to show your daughter. That's a stronger position than judging him sight unseen.
